AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_17102> "A compound in which one or more of the OH groups of phosphoric acid have been replaced with an amino or substituted amino group. The term is commonly confined to the phosphoric triamides, P(=O)(NR<small><sub>2</sub></small>)<small><sub>3</sub></small>, since replacement of one or two OH groups produces phosphoramidic acids: P(=O)(OH)(NR<small><sub>2</sub></small>)<small><sub>2</sub></small> , P(=O)(OH)<small><sub>2</sub></small>(NR<small><sub>2</sub></small>).")
