# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_35705> (immunosuppressive agent)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_35705> "An agent that suppresses immune function by one of several mechanisms of action. Classical cytotoxic immunosuppressants act by inhibiting DNA synthesis. Others may act through activation of T-cells or by inhibiting the activation of helper cells. In addition, an immunosuppressive agent is a role played by a compound which is exhibited by a capability to diminish the extent and/or voracity of an immune response.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#id> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_35705> "CHEBI:35705")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_35705> "immunosuppressive agent")
