# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_7071> (N,N-diethyl-m-toluamide)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_7071> "A monocarboxylic acid amide resulting from the formal condensation of the carboxy group of <em>m</em>-toluic acid with the nitrogen of diethylamine. First developed by the U.S. Army in 1946 for use by military personnel in insect-infested areas, it is the most widely used insect repellent worldwide.")
